# The Gradle wrapper IS committed, unlike in Flutter's default template.
#
# Flutter's template ignores gradlew/gradlew.bat/gradle-wrapper.jar because `flutter build` drives
# Gradle through its own tooling and never invokes the wrapper. But that leaves the repository
# unable to run Gradle directly — `./gradlew :app:testDebugUnitTest` in CI fails with
# "No such file or directory" — and leaves the Gradle version unpinned for anyone who does.
# Committing it is the standard Android convention; CI validates the jar's checksum against
# Gradle's published hashes via gradle/actions/wrapper-validation.

/.gradle
/captures/
/local.properties
GeneratedPluginRegistrant.java
.cxx/

# Build output.
/build/

# Remember to never publicly share your keystore.
# See https://flutter.dev/to/reference-keystore
key.properties
**/*.keystore
**/*.jks
